NAME

ulibClearMem - Clears an area of memory


SYNOPSIS

void ulibClearMem(UBYTE *Memory, long Size)
                       a0           d0


DESCRIPTION

This function clears a block of memory of size <Size> starting at <Memory>.


NOTES

While this function will always be supported, it is recommended that your C
compiler's bzero() or memset() function be used instead.  These functions are
usually inlined by the compiler for faster operation.

Under Xenolink Z.4 this function is not optimised for clearing large memory
blocks.
